<%# The from-emerged sweep's held-out confirmatory reading (docs/design_record.md, 2026-09-25,
    "The from-emerged economy arms, confirmed on held-out parents"): `reading` is the sweep's
    Lab::DescendantReading::Report, whose `heldout` this section prints and whose `final` it
    shares. The per-child rows stay in `lab:from_emerged_heldout_report`. %>
<% heldout = reading.heldout %>
<section class="mt-6" id="heldout-reading">
  <h2>
    A held-out confirmatory reading, pre-registered 2026-09-25
    <% if heldout.any? %>
      <span class="badge <%= reading.interim? ? 'badge-warning' : 'badge-success' %>">
        <%= reading.interim? ? "interim" : "final" %>
      </span>
    <% end %>
  </h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted">
    Its rules were written after the reading above and an exploratory look at the same children,
    so they are read only on the children of parents from sweep 9's extension (seeds above
    <%= Lab::FromEmergedHeldout::LAST_SEEN_SEED %>) none of whose children had been seen.
    Past a settling window of <%= number_with_delimiter Lab::FromEmergedHeldout::SETTLING_WINDOW %> epochs,
    a child relapsed where its share sat below
    <%= percent_value Lab::FromEmergedHeldout::RELAPSE_SHARE %> for
    <%= Lab::FromEmergedHeldout::RELAPSE_RUN %> samples running; it is extinct where its last-decile
    median share is below <%= percent_value Lab::FromEmergedHeldout::EXTINCT_SHARE %>.
    H3-latency pairs the economy child against the continuation child on the ratio of their
    last-decile to first-decile median <span class="mono">copy_latency</span>, a lower ratio
    favouring its side; H4-survivors reads the original complexity rule on pairs whose two children
    both survived. Host mode is not re-tested.
  </p>

  <% if heldout.any? %>
    <figure class="table-figure mt-4">
      <figcaption class="table-caption text-sm text-muted" id="heldout-treatments">
        Held-out children per treatment, read so far.
      </figcaption>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="heldout-treatments">
        <table class="data-table" aria-labelledby="heldout-treatments">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Treatment</th>
              <th class="numeric">Children</th>
              <th class="numeric">Finished</th>
              <th class="numeric">Settled relapses</th>
              <th class="numeric">Extinct</th>
              <th class="numeric">Latency measured</th>
              <th class="numeric">Survivors</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <% heldout.arms.each do |arm| %>
              <tr>
                <td><%= arm.name %></td>
                <td class="numeric"><%= arm.children.size %></td>
                <td class="numeric"><%= arm.finished_count %></td>
                <td class="numeric"><%= arm.settled_relapse_count %></td>
                <td class="numeric"><%= arm.extinct_count %></td>
                <td class="numeric"><%= arm.latency_measured_count %></td>
                <td class="numeric"><%= arm.survivor_count %></td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </figure>

    <h3 class="mt-4">Hypotheses</h3>
    <ul>
      <% heldout.tests.each do |test| %>
        <% comparison = test.comparison %>
        <li class="mb-3">
          <strong><%= test.hypothesis %></strong>, <%= test.treatment.name %> against the continuation:
          <span class="badge <%= test.badge_class %>"><%= test.outcome_label %></span>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">
            <%= pluralize(comparison.measured_count, "pair") %> measured on both sides:
            <%= comparison.favouring %> favour the treatment, <%= comparison.against %> the continuation,
            <%= comparison.ties %> tie<% if comparison.p_value %>; one-sided sign test
            p = <%= metric_value comparison.p_value.to_f %><% end %>.
            <% if comparison.carried_by.any? %>
              Carried by parents
              <%= comparison.carried_by.map { |parents| parents.map { |id| "run #{id}" }.join(" and ") }.to_sentence(two_words_connector: " or ", last_word_connector: ", or ") %>:
              without their pairs the test falls to p ≥ <%= Lab::FromEmergedHeldout::SIGN_TEST_LEVEL %>.
            <% end %>
          </p>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  <% else %>
    <p class="mt-4">No held-out child yet.</p>
  <% end %>
</section>
